## ShellCheck config for the msgcollector package.
##
## msgcollector scripts source helper-scripts (get_colors.sh, has.bsh,
## check_runtime.bsh, ...) by absolute HELPER_SCRIPTS_PATH. In an isolated
## staged/CI check those siblings are not on disk, so shellcheck cannot follow
## them and reports vars they define as unset. Suppress only those cross-source
## false positives; real dead code is removed at the source instead.
##
##   SC2154 - var referenced but not assigned (assigned in a sourced file).
##   SC2034 - var assigned but "unused": read cross-file, incl. command-name
##            indirection (error_handler runs '$output_x'/'$output_cli').
##   SC1090 - cannot follow a non-constant source (HELPER_SCRIPTS_PATH path).
##   SC1091 - not following: sourced file absent in the isolated checkout.
disable=SC2154
disable=SC2034
disable=SC1090
disable=SC1091
